from pathlib import Path
from html import escape as e
import json, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP

OUT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT=OUT.parent
SAAS=ROOT.parent/'hexplain-saas'
ENGINE=ROOT.parent/'hexplain-tools'
# Read the original finding catalog without regenerating or overwriting the original report.
catalog={'__file__':str(OUT/'build_report.py')}
exec((OUT/'build_report.py').read_text(encoding='utf-8').split('def refs_html')[0],catalog)
fixes={
'S01':('Fixed','Pinned Next 15.5.25 and React 19.2.4; updated transitive packages and lockfile. The current full npm audit reports zero known vulnerabilities.','npm audit; frontend build and workflow tests'),
'M01':('Fixed','Numeric comparisons preserve integer precision, including uint64 values. Mixed comparisons use the represented floating value without first rounding the integer to Double. NaN, infinities and signed zero have explicit behavior.','NumericCorrectnessTest; ReviewRegressionTest'),
'M02':('Fixed','Signed 64-bit arithmetic is checked. Overflow, fractional indexes, oversized substring indexes and shifts outside 0–63 fail explicitly; left shifts cannot silently wrap. Unsigned values outside the arithmetic range are rejected before narrowing.','NumericCorrectnessTest; core suite'),
'M03':('Fixed','HEL now explicitly defines integer division as truncation toward zero and fractional division when a floating operand is present. BMP stride remains integer arithmetic; the gamma example uses 100000.0 to retain fractions. Bundled DLV resources are synchronized.','BMP golden vectors for widths 0–130; specification gates'),
'M04':('Fixed','Null inequality now follows the normative table; null equality remains consistent.','NumericCorrectnessTest; ReviewRegressionTest'),
'S02':('Fixed','A structural fallback compares every IR field, with explicit semantic exclusions. Reachability includes dispatch and data-layout types. Unknown parsing changes default to breaking instead of disappearing from the version gate.','ProfileDiffer tests; ReviewRegressionTest'),
'S03':('Fixed','Conditional presence changes and added dispatch alternatives are conservatively breaking. Publication no longer treats an unproven conditional addition as compatible.','ProfileDiffer tests; ReviewRegressionTest'),
'S04':('Fixed','Version labels must be canonical major.minor.patch with bounded nonnegative components. Invalid labels fail before compilation; compatibility failures fail closed.','PublishIntegrityTest; ReviewRegressionTest'),
'S05':('Fixed','Run comparison requires successful runs for the same file, format and workspace. Failure cannot be interpreted as an empty successful result or an improvement.','ReviewRegressionTest; RunService checks'),
'S06':('Fixed','Cached computation is copied with the current workspace, file ID, filename and finding attribution. Cache reuse does not inherit another request’s identity.','ReviewRegressionTest'),
'S07':('Scoped mitigation','Authentication, server-owned workspace authorization, CSRF protection and object-level checks protect the implemented single-workspace deployment. The backend binds to loopback by default. This does not implement production multi-tenant identity, RBAC or database isolation.','SecurityBoundaryTest; authenticated HTTP smoke'),
'V01':('Fixed','Video rate/duration/count/channel shapes reject invalid numeric types and ranges. Ratios reject zero components. Valid integer rates and unsigned frame counts remain accepted.','15 video numeric/rational cases through the family validator'),
'V02':('Fixed','The shared shape loader now discovers all vocabulary modules, including video, geospatial and aspect constraints. The document shape no longer incorrectly targets every ontology’s creator metadata.','11 specification gates; family-validator fixtures'),
'S08':('Fixed','Version, run and finding IDs retain full UUIDs. Repositories reject duplicate identities instead of silently replacing records.','PublishIntegrityTest'),
'S09':('Fixed','The in-process publish transaction serializes predecessor selection, version checking and save. Duplicate published format/version pairs are rejected. Distributed publication requires a transactional datastore.','Four concurrent same-version attempts: exactly one published winner'),
'S10':('Fixed','Provenance fingerprints the actual core, HDL and adapter artifacts. Failed runs retain attempted file/rule hashes and engine identity. CI pins the engine revision and applies the reviewed patch.','PublishIntegrityTest; ReviewRegressionTest; patch reverse-check'),
'S11':('Fixed','Raw mapping cards are explicitly previews; a separate RDF panel displays the engine’s actual semantic graph. Computed values and datatypes are tested. An integration regression also fixed field-level HDL value expressions to resolve against instance rather than parent.','SemanticGraphTest; HDL emission test; HTTP typed-view check'),
'U01':('Fixed','Viewer and comparison effects discard superseded responses and reset stale results. Findings deep-link to the pinned profile and byte offset.','Out-of-order comparison regression; frontend typecheck'),
'U02':('Fixed','Compilation and publication have separate states and labels. Editing invalidates compile results; pending actions disable relevant inputs.','Studio state-transition regression'),
'U03':('Scoped mitigation','The viewer supports files up to 1 MiB and renders 1,024 bytes per page without a per-byte ownership array. The raw-byte endpoint returns bounded ranges. Larger-file streaming is not implemented.','Viewer pagination regression; HTTP page/range validation'),
'U04':('Implemented; manual validation pending','Tree roles, roving focus, keyboard expansion/navigation, accessible mapping buttons, selected-byte scrolling and scoped shortcuts are implemented. Mobile navigation supports Escape and focus return. Screen-reader and visual browser checks were unavailable.','Keyboard component regression; source review'),
'V03':('Fixed','Positive integer numerator/denominator terms preserve rates such as 30000/1001 and 24000/1001 exactly. Paired-value shapes reject incomplete or zero-denominator rates. Documentation distinguishes nominal rate from variable-rate timing and does not infer duration from it.','Rational SHACL vectors; synchronized vocabulary documentation'),
'G01':('Implemented; remote CI pending','Added specification and platform CI, Python dependency pins, a reproducible engine revision plus patch, expected-correctness regressions and frontend checks. Local suites and HTTP integration passed. The new workflow has not run on a remote clean runner in this session.','11 gates; 687 JVM tests; 3 frontend tests; 9 HTTP checks'),
}
assert len(fixes)==len(catalog['findings'])==23

def source(root,rel):
    p=root/rel
    assert p.is_file(),p
    href=Path(__import__('os').path.relpath(p,OUT)).as_posix()
    return f'<a href="{e(href)}">{e(root.name+"/"+rel)}</a>'

scores=[('Correctness & mathematical contracts',30,9,8.5,'Explicit numeric, array and georeferencing contracts with regression evidence; no formal proof or universal GDAL coverage.'),('Architecture & maintainability',20,8.5,8,'Ontology layers, concept separation and versioned draft models improved; SaaS ports remain strong. Reflective IR comparison still needs maintenance discipline.'),('Validation & test evidence',20,9,8,'Family SHACL meta-validation, 40 geospatial cases and 121 exact affine round trips; only three frontend workflows and no manual browser audit.'),('UX & accessibility',15,7.5,7.5,'Clearer states, bounded views and keyboard controls; visual and screen-reader validation remain outstanding.'),('Delivery & operational readiness',15,8.5,4,'CI and dependency pins improve reproducibility. SaaS still uses volatile storage and has no isolated worker or production tenancy stack.')]
spec=float((sum(Decimal(w)*Decimal(str(s)) for _,w,s,a,_ in scores)/100).quantize(Decimal('.01'),rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))
saas=float((sum(Decimal(w)*Decimal(str(a)) for _,w,s,a,_ in scores)/100).quantize(Decimal('.01'),rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))
rows=''.join(f'<tr><th scope="row">{e(n)}</th><td>{w}%</td><td>{s:g}</td><td>{a:g}</td><td>{e(reason)}</td></tr>' for n,w,s,a,reason in scores)
cards=''
for f in catalog['findings']:
    status,fix,test=fixes[f['id']]
    refs=' · '.join(dict.fromkeys(source(root,rel) for root,rel,_ in f['refs']))
    cards+=f'<article id="{f["id"]}" data-search="{e((f["id"]+" "+f["title"]+" "+fix).lower())}"><div class="meta">{f["id"]} · original {f["severity"]} <span class="badge">{e(status)}</span></div><h3>{e(f["title"])}</h3><p>{e(fix)}</p><p class="evidence"><b>Verification:</b> {e(test)}</p><details><summary>Source files</summary><p class="paths">{refs}</p></details></article>'

html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Hexplain — fixes & second review · 5 September 2026</title><style>
:root{{--ink:#172e38;--muted:#516875;--paper:#f2f5f4;--line:#d6e2df;--accent:#007367}}*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.65 system-ui,Segoe UI,sans-serif}}a{{color:var(--accent);text-underline-offset:3px}}header{{background:#102f39;color:white;padding:60px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1120px)/2)) 48px}}header p{{max-width:850px;color:#d7e5e8}}h1{{font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,60px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-1.5px;margin:18px 0 24px}}h2{{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2}}h3{{font-size:21px;line-height:1.35;margin:12px 0}}main{{max-width:1168px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px 60px}}nav{{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}}section{{margin:38px 0 48px}}.eyebrow,.meta{{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.7px;font-weight:750;text-transform:uppercase}}.stats{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px}}.stat,article,.panel{{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:24px}}.stat strong{{font-size:38px;display:block;line-height:1.3}}.stat span,.muted{{color:var(--muted)}}.delta{{color:var(--accent);font-size:14px}}.callout{{background:#fff4e8;border-left:5px solid #b76b26;padding:20px 26px;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}}th,td{{padding:13px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left;vertical-align:top}}thead{{background:#e4eeeb}}.tablewrap{{overflow:auto}}article{{margin:16px 0;scroll-margin-top:20px}}article p{{margin:12px 0}}.badge{{display:inline-block;margin-left:8px;background:#e5f1eb;color:#235c47;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:5px;font-size:11px}}.evidence{{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}}.paths{{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:12px}}details{{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:10px}}summary{{cursor:pointer;font-size:14px}}.cols{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}}li{{margin:8px 0}}button,input{{font:inherit;border:1px solid #7b9695;background:white;padding:10px 14px;border-radius:6px;color:var(--ink)}}input{{width:min(100%,650px)}}button{{cursor:pointer}}:focus-visible{{outline:3px solid #069387;outline-offset:3px}}footer{{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:24px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}}code{{font:14px Consolas,monospace}}@media(max-width:760px){{.stats{{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}.cols{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}header{{padding:35px 24px}}.stat{{padding:18px}}.stat strong{{font-size:31px}}}}@media print{{body{{background:white;font-size:11px}}header{{background:white;color:var(--ink);padding:20px}}header p{{color:var(--ink)}}main{{padding:0}}nav,.controls{{display:none}}article{{break-inside:avoid}}h1{{font-size:34px}}h2{{font-size:23px}}.stat strong{{font-size:28px}}}}
</style></head><body><header><div class="eyebrow">Engineering review / follow-up / 05 September 2026</div><h1>Hexplain, after the fixes.</h1><p>Numerical contracts, validation coverage, publication integrity and semantic output are substantially stronger. All 23 original findings have an implementation response; scoped mitigations and unverified acceptance checks are identified below.</p></header><main>
<nav aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#scores">Scores</a><a href="#math">Mathematics</a><a href="#verification">Verification</a><a href="#findings">23 findings</a><a href="#remaining">Remaining work</a><a href="original.html">Original review</a></nav>
<section class="stats" aria-label="Results"><div class="stat"><span>Specification quality</span><strong>{spec:.2f}/10</strong><div class="delta">Previously 6.15 · +{spec-6.15:.2f}</div></div><div class="stat"><span>SaaS quality</span><strong>{saas:.2f}/10</strong><div class="delta">Previously 5.05 · +{saas-5.05:.2f}</div></div><div class="stat"><span>JVM + frontend test cases</span><strong>690</strong><div class="delta">687 JVM + 3 frontend</div></div><div class="stat"><span>Known npm vulnerabilities</span><strong>0</strong><div class="delta">Full audit at review time</div></div></section>
<p class="callout"><b>Release interpretation:</b> this is an authenticated, single-workspace application with in-memory state and a 1 MiB interactive-view limit. The fixes do not make it a production multi-tenant SaaS. Mathematical correctness is supported by explicit contracts and regression evidence, not certified by a formal proof or independent implementation.</p>
<section id="ontology-revision"><h2>Ontology and GDAL revision</h2><p><b>Specification: 8.13 ? 8.60/10.</b> The 1.1 working drafts add reusable grids, bands, calibration, masks, arbitrary-rank arrays, complete affine and rational-polynomial metadata, and separate Z/M flags. Ontology entities no longer use SKOS concept-matching assertions. New metadata and SHACL meta-validation gates enforce those boundaries.</p><p>Coverage is now tracked against <b>246 documentation pages from GDAL 3.13.3</b>, with source hashes and explicit verification status. These are inventory entries, not 246 supported binary formats. Forty new semantic validation cases and 121 exact affine round trips pass. All 14 specification gates and the engine/backend suites pass; the final repeated-axis correction has separate affected-gate evidence.</p><p><a href="../specification/coverage/index.html">GDAL coverage and remaining gaps</a> ? <a href="../specification/ontology-design/index.html">Ontology modeling policy and 10/10 acceptance bar</a> ? <a href="ontology-gates.log">Full gate run</a> ? <a href="ontology-final-checks.log">Final affected checks</a> ? <a href="ontology-engine-tests.log">Engine suites</a> ? <a href="ontology-saas-tests.log">Backend suite</a> ? <a href="post-fixes.html">Previous 8.13 review</a></p><p class="callout">A 10/10 claim is not justified yet. Remaining evidence includes driver-specific binary corpora, independent interoperability review, database traversal/runtime-schema implementations and broader accessibility validation. New semantic terms do not implement new binary decoders.</p></section><section id="term-documentation"><h2>Complete term and shape documentation</h2><p>The reference now documents <b>730 named resources across 35 modules, including 93 named shapes</b>. Each entry includes a label, definition, usage scope, owning vocabulary, type, declared domain/range or an explicit absence statement, and validation context. Anonymous property constraints, logical alternatives, cardinalities and queries are expanded under their owning shapes. A reading guide distinguishes inference, validation and rule execution.</p><p>Definitions and scope notes are canonical RDF annotations. The documentation gate verifies complete coverage, fragment links, generated content and the annotation-only boundary. All 15 specification gates and 687 engine/backend tests pass; the final documentation checks also pass. The engine bundle and pinned SaaS patch include the same annotations. This documentation pass does not change the existing quality score or claim additional decoder coverage.</p><p><a href="../specification/reference/index.html">Complete reference and reading guide</a> ? <a href="../specification/reference/README.md">Authoring workflow</a> ? <a href="term-documentation-gates.log">15 specification gates</a> ? <a href="term-documentation-final-checks.log">Final documentation checks</a> ? <a href="term-documentation-engine-tests.log">Engine/backend tests</a></p></section><section id="scores"><h2>Revised quality scores</h2><p>The original weights are unchanged. Scores are reviewer judgments, not coverage percentages: 0–2 unsafe/incomplete, 3–4 significant gaps, 5–6 useful prototype, 7–8 robust engineering, 9–10 independently well-verified. Improvements reflect working fixes; delivery and accessibility deductions remain.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Weight</th><th>Spec /10</th><th>SaaS /10</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}<tr><th>Weighted total</th><td>100%</td><th>{spec:.2f}</th><th>{saas:.2f}</th><td>Σ(weight × dimension score) / 100</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="math"><h2>Mathematical correctness</h2><div class="cols"><div class="panel"><h3>Numerics and layout</h3><ul><li>Adjacent integers above 2⁵³ compare distinctly; uint64 comparisons retain exact values.</li><li>Signed 64-bit overflow fails instead of wrapping. Integer-only 5 / 2 = 2 and −5 / 2 = −2; 5 / 2.0 = 2.5.</li><li>Fractional indexes and invalid shifts fail. Unicode ordering compares code points; NaN and null behavior are explicit.</li><li>BMP row stride uses 4 × floor((width × bitsPerPixel + 31) / 32) for nonnegative integer inputs. Golden vectors cover widths 0–130.</li></ul></div><div class="panel"><h3>Timing and semantics</h3><ul><li>30000/1001 and 24000/1001 remain exact rational rates. Zero or missing denominators are invalid.</li><li>Negative duration/rate/counts and malformed ratios are rejected by the family validator.</li><li>Nominal rate is not used to infer variable-frame-rate duration.</li><li>The semantic integration test maps raw 100 to typed RDF integer 10, retaining raw 100 in the parse tree.</li></ul></div></div><p class="muted">These checks establish the tested behavior. They do not exhaust every expression, parser layout, codec, RDF mapping or SHACL interaction. Exhaustive conformance, fuzzing and a second implementation remain useful assurance work.</p></section>
<section id="verification"><h2>Verification evidence</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Engine core / HDL</th><td>412 / 223 passed; zero failures or skips</td><td><a href="ontology-final-engine-tests.log">Combined Gradle log</a></td></tr><tr><th>SaaS backend</th><td>52 passed, including publish races, authorization and semantic output</td><td><a href="ontology-final-engine-tests.log">Combined Gradle log</a></td></tr><tr><th>Frontend</th><td>3 component workflow tests passed; TypeScript check passed</td><td><a href="frontend-tests.log">Vitest log</a></td></tr><tr><th>Production compilation</th><td>Next production build passed</td><td><a href="frontend-build-final.log">Build log</a></td></tr><tr><th>Specification</th><td>14/14 gates; all 77 Turtle files parse; 15 video and 40 geospatial/array cases</td><td><a href="ontology-gates.log">Gate log</a></td></tr><tr><th>Authenticated HTTP flow</th><td>9 checks passed through the Next proxy, including login, validation, RDF and byte bounds</td><td><a href="http-smoke-results.json">Results</a> · <a href="http_smoke.py">Reproducible script</a></td></tr><tr><th>Dependencies</th><td>0 known npm vulnerabilities at audit time</td><td><a href="npm-audit-after.json">Audit JSON</a></td></tr><tr><th>Patch / whitespace</th><td>Engine patch reverse-check and repository diff checks passed</td><td>Local Git checks</td></tr><tr><th>Not performed</th><td colspan="2">Remote CI execution, deployed-environment testing, browser screenshots, screen-reader audit, penetration test and full mathematical proof. Browser automation was unavailable.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The viewer test’s timeout was raised to 15 seconds after contention during concurrent builds; its assertions were retained and it passed on rerun. A genuine semantic-mapping failure was fixed in the HDL emitter before the final passing suite.</p></section>
<section id="findings"><h2>Disposition of all 23 original findings</h2><p>19 are marked fixed, two have explicit supported-scope mitigations, and two are implemented with manual or remote verification pending. Each original priority remains visible for traceability.</p><div class="controls"><label for="search">Filter findings</label><br><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="ID, topic, or implementation…"><p id="count" aria-live="polite">23 findings</p></div>{cards}</section>
<section id="remaining"><h2>Remaining work before a production SaaS release</h2><ol><li><b>Durability and concurrency across processes.</b> Replace in-memory repositories with transactions, unique constraints, migrations, backup and recovery. Current publication serialization is scoped to one application process.</li><li><b>Production identity and execution boundaries.</b> Add tenant-aware identity, RBAC, quotas, worker isolation/timeouts, operational monitoring and HTTPS/session configuration appropriate to the deployment.</li><li><b>Broader UX acceptance.</b> Perform keyboard-only and screen-reader walkthroughs in a real browser, responsive visual checks and large-file performance measurements. Files above 1 MiB need a streaming architecture.</li><li><b>Independent correctness assurance.</b> Run new CI on a clean remote checkout, add differential/property testing and parser fuzzing, and upstream the engine patch into a versioned release.</li><li><b>Documentation polish.</b> Continue first-run onboarding and static documentation/accessibility improvements beyond the numbered defects.</li></ol><p>These limitations constrain the score and prevent a production-readiness claim. They are not silently counted as completed features.</p></section>
<section><h2>Using the fixed application</h2><p>Configure backend credentials, start both services, then sign in at the frontend’s <code>/login</code>. For a fresh checkout, use the pinned sibling engine revision and apply its reviewed patch exactly once. The current workspace already contains it.</p><p>{source(SAAS,'REVIEW-FIXES.md')} · {source(SAAS,'engine-revision.txt')} · {source(SAAS,'engine-patches/review-correctness.patch')}</p></section>
<footer>Review scope: local working changes in hexplain.io, hexplain-saas and the shared hexplain-tools engine. Base commits: 0cae353 / f9f3fec / df717d2. Changes are uncommitted and not deployed. The original review is preserved separately. Generated 2026-09-05; scores describe this snapshot.</footer></main><script>const search=document.getElementById('search');search.addEventListener('input',()=>{{let n=0;document.querySelectorAll('article[data-search]').forEach(a=>{{a.hidden=!a.dataset.search.includes(search.value.toLowerCase());if(!a.hidden)n++}});document.getElementById('count').textContent=n+' findings';}});</script></body></html>'''
(OUT/'index.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print(json.dumps({'spec_score':spec,'saas_score':saas,'findings':len(fixes),'html_bytes':len(html.encode())}))
